# The stem's files this node carries MODIFIED, each with the reason it differs.
#
# WHAT THIS IS FOR. `.offshoot-omissions` lists what this repo does not carry
# from its stem; this lists what it carries and changes. Everything else is the
# stem's byte for byte or this repo's own, so a diff against the stem reads as:
# the additions, the omissions (listed there) and these. A modified file is a
# conflict on every cascade that touches it, so each one here is a cost paid on
# purpose, and the reason says what it buys. A cascade reviewer meeting one of
# these files knows the node's side is a decision; meeting any other modified
# file, it is drift.
#
# AND IT IS CHECKED, by `scripts/check-divergences.mjs` (the tree's one copy,
# from template-svelte), run by `web/test/offshoot-divergences.test.ts` and by
# `scripts/apply-omissions.sh` during a merge: it fails on a modified file with
# no entry, on an entry whose file no longer differs, and on an entry with no
# reason. A file at the stem's OLD version is drift, not a divergence:
# `scripts/check-stem-drift.mjs` catches that.
#
# FORMAT. One file per line: its path, then its reason. `#` starts a comment.
# A line `[<branch>]` starts a section; this repo has one node, `main`, so it
# has none: every entry is what template-svelte-docs `main` modifies from
# template-svelte-shadcn `main`. A child REPO never keeps these entries: its
# list is its own, written against this repo, and until it writes one it
# carries this file unchanged and the check says it has none.

# The workspace
.offshoot-omissions            this repo's own entry: the home page `+page.svelte`, which would hide the content's own `index.md`
AGENTS.md                      the template's rules, then the docs engine's (its three layers, content never compiled as Svelte, dead links failing the build)
README.md                      the docs template's README: the engine, the content folder and what a site changes
pnpm-lock.yaml                 the lockfile with the docs engine's dependencies
web/package.json               the docs engine's dependencies (the unified Markdown pipeline, Shiki, Pagefind, github-slugger), and bits-ui and lucide newer than the stem's (a bump whose home is template-svelte-shadcn)
web/svelte.config.js           the docs config loaded, and the prerender crawl told about the content's public files, copied in after the build
web/vite.plugins.ts            the docs engine's Vite plugin, beside Tailwind, in the slot every repo puts its plugins

# The site
web/src/app.css                the docs' styles: the page background all the way down, the prose on the theme tokens, code blocks and search excerpts
web/src/web-config.json        the template's name and description as a docs site
web/src/lib/index.ts           the docs (the generated manifest and loaders) and the site search, composed with the app
web/src/routes/+layout.svelte  the mode watcher on the system preference (the stem's dark default dropped, for a light theme), and the site header, the page in `<main>` and the search dialog; the overlay layers as the stem's
web/src/routes/+error.svelte   the error page on shadcn's button, with the docs' navigation back
